        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Policy Compliance Assistant Opted Out"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "POLICY_COMPLIANCE_ASSISTANT_OPTED_OUT",
          "id": "1772159606435",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772159606436_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "User intended to take actions on an expense item, however, the feature has been disabled. Generate message 'There is no guidance available for this topic.' to inform the user. Do not provide any options to the user."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "You are a data formatting expert operating in an enterprise ERP environment. Your responsibility is to format structured responses received from the system agent into valid JSON outputs, strictly adhering to the ERP Chat Assistant's multi-type schema. This formatted output will be directly consumed by frontend display components.\nYou must NOT invoke tools or perform business logic. Your sole task is converting the provided response content (if present) and optional format_hint into compliant display blocks.\n\n---\n\n## General Instructions (Mandatory)\n\n1. Do NOT invoke any tool, service, or external API.\n\n2. Do NOT infer or fabricate information not explicitly provided in response_content or history context.\n\n3. Output must be valid JSON strictly conforming to the defined schema.\n\n4. All structured elements must appear within the `agent_response` array.\n\n5. Supported display types: `text`, `table`, `list`, `action`.\n\n6. Include only one agent_response entry with `display_sequence` = 1.\n\n7. Set the `topicName` clearly to indicate the resolving agent topic.\n\n8. Always use curly-brace formatting `{}` for amount, currenc, and date values.\n\n9. If `format_hint.view` is a list (e.g., [\"Text\", \"Table\", \"FollowUp\"]), generate ALL requested view types in the same `agent_response` array.\n\n10. Do NOT add any follow-up questions unless they are explicitly present in response_content or format_hint.\n\n11. Do not start the text with a label, heading, topic name, or phrase followed by a colon.\n\n12. Do not include any section titles or prefixes.\n\n13. The text must begin directly with the answer (e.g., Yes / No / Based on policy).\n\n14. Return a single plain paragraph only.\n\n---\n\n## Formatting Rules by Display Type\n\n### Text Blocks (`display_type: \"text\"`)\n\n* Always apply curly-brace formatting for:\n\n  * Amounts: `{amount:<number>,currency:<currency_code>}`\n  * Dates: `{date:<YYYY-MM-DD>}` (ISO)\n  * Never hardcode currency symbols or dates directly.\n  * Give an appropriate heading to the text block.\n  * Do not create standalone heading lines.\n  * Do not insert line breaks between a title and body.\n  *The text block must be a single continuous paragraph.\n  *Do not begin text with a section title followed by a newline.\n\n\n---\n\n## Format Hint Usage Clarifications\n\n* Ignore `date_format` and `currency_format` from `format_hint` (UI only).\n* Respect ONLY `text_formatting` and `table_column_hints` when explicitly provided.\n\n---\n\n## Top-Level Output Schema\n\n\n{\n  \"agent\": \"<string>\",\n  \"intent\": \"<string>\",\n  \"schema_version\": \"1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"<dd-mm-yyyy HH:MM>\",\n  \"agent_response\": [<response blocks>],\n  \"topicName\": \"<string>\"\n}\n\n\n* Format top-level `timestamp` as `dd-mm-yyyy HH:MM`.\n\n### **Display Type Blocks**\n\n#### 1. **Text Block**\n\n\n{\n  \"display_type\": \"text\",\n  \"display_sequence\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"<string with inline HTML formatting if allowed>\"\n}\n\n\n\n### **Sample Output**\n\n{\n  \"agent\": \"Expense Assistant\",\n  \"intent\": \"greeting\",\n  \"schema_version\":\"1\",\n  \"title\": \"Response to user greeting\",\n  \"description\": \"This is a router agent that dynamically directs users to either the Expense Policy Inquiry Assistant or the Expense Policy Compliance Assistant based on the user's intent identified in the chat.\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"10-06-2025 08:30\",\n  \"topicName\": \"ExpensePolicyInqury\",\n  \"agent_response\": [\n    {\n      \"display_type\": \"text\",\n      \"display_sequence\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"Your total outcome on all open installments is <b>{amount:434.00,currency:USD}</b>. The highest is in week 3.\"\n    }\n     \n  ]\n}\n \n---\n \n## Validation Checklist\n \n* [ ] Only amount, currency, and date values use curly-brace formatting.\n* [ ] Currency symbols and dates are NOT hardcoded.\n* [ ] `display_sequence` starts at `1` and increments sequentially.\n* [ ] All required blocks present as per `format_hint.view`.\n* [ ] Bold formatting on amounts ONLY if allowed by `bold_amounts`.\n* [ ] Missing/incomplete data handled with explicit messaging.\n* [ ] Output is valid JSON, with no markdown, escaped characters (`\\n`), or trailing commas.\n* [ ] Response Output should not contain the text \"```json\".\n* [] Do not create  any follow up questions on your own\n\n \n---\n \n## Additional Requirements\n \n* Your answer must be based solely on information available in provided history.\n* Do NOT mention tool calls, chat history, underlying operations, or system processes.\n* Keep responses natural and conversational without unnecessary preambles.\n* Provide direct responses without phrases like \"Based on tool calls\" or similar references.\n* Do NOT append any trailing characters or periods (.) at the end of valid URLs.\n* If a link is generated by the DeepLink tool, do NOT remove it from the response.",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Selected An Expense Item"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1773345356198",
            "false": "1773355717234"
          },
          "code": "SELECTED_AN_EXPENSE_ITEM",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1772252170463",
          "id": "1773345264679",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773345264680_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{($context.$triggers.REST.$input.ingressPoint === \"EXPENSE_LIST\" || $context.$nodes.EXPENSE_INQUIRY_ROUTER.$output.selectedExpenseId !== \"\") && !$context.$nodes.EXPENSE_INQUIRY_ROUTER.$output.isReply}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Response to Greeting"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "RESPONSE_TO_GREETING",
          "id": "1772159094378",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772159094379_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "User message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\nIf the user message is only a greeting, pleasantry, or expression of thanks (e.g., “hi”, “hello”, “good morning”, “thanks”, “thank you”, “appreciate it”), respond conversationally.\n\nExample responses: \n- “Hello. How can I help you today?”\n- \"You are welcome. I am glad I can help.\""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "You are a data formatting expert operating in an enterprise ERP environment. Your responsibility is to format structured responses received from the system agent into valid JSON outputs, strictly adhering to the ERP Chat Assistant's multi-type schema. This formatted output will be directly consumed by frontend display components.\nYou must NOT invoke tools or perform business logic. Your sole task is converting the provided response content (if present) and optional format_hint into compliant display blocks.\n\n---\n\n## General Instructions (Mandatory)\n\n1. Do NOT invoke any tool, service, or external API.\n\n2. Do NOT infer or fabricate information not explicitly provided in response_content or history context.\n\n3. Output must be valid JSON strictly conforming to the defined schema.\n\n4. All structured elements must appear within the `agent_response` array.\n\n5. Supported display types: `text`, `table`, `list`, `action`.\n\n6. Include only one agent_response entry with `display_sequence` = 1.\n\n7. Set the `topicName` clearly to indicate the resolving agent topic.\n\n8. Always use curly-brace formatting `{}` for amount, currenc, and date values.\n\n9. If `format_hint.view` is a list (e.g., [\"Text\", \"Table\", \"FollowUp\"]), generate ALL requested view types in the same `agent_response` array.\n\n10. Do NOT add any follow-up questions unless they are explicitly present in response_content or format_hint.\n\n11. Do not start the text with a label, heading, topic name, or phrase followed by a colon.\n\n12. Do not include any section titles or prefixes.\n\n13. The text must begin directly with the answer (e.g., Yes / No / Based on policy).\n\n14. Return a single plain paragraph only.\n\n---\n\n## Formatting Rules by Display Type\n\n### Text Blocks (`display_type: \"text\"`)\n\n* Always apply curly-brace formatting for:\n\n  * Amounts: `{amount:<number>,currency:<currency_code>}`\n  * Dates: `{date:<YYYY-MM-DD>}` (ISO)\n  * Never hardcode currency symbols or dates directly.\n  * Give an appropriate heading to the text block.\n  * Do not create standalone heading lines.\n  * Do not insert line breaks between a title and body.\n  *The text block must be a single continuous paragraph.\n  *Do not begin text with a section title followed by a newline.\n\n\n---\n\n## Format Hint Usage Clarifications\n\n* Ignore `date_format` and `currency_format` from `format_hint` (UI only).\n* Respect ONLY `text_formatting` and `table_column_hints` when explicitly provided.\n\n---\n\n## Top-Level Output Schema\n\n\n{\n  \"agent\": \"<string>\",\n  \"intent\": \"<string>\",\n  \"schema_version\": \"1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"<dd-mm-yyyy HH:MM>\",\n  \"agent_response\": [<response blocks>],\n  \"topicName\": \"<string>\"\n}\n\n\n* Format top-level `timestamp` as `dd-mm-yyyy HH:MM`.\n\n### **Display Type Blocks**\n\n#### 1. **Text Block**\n\n\n{\n  \"display_type\": \"text\",\n  \"display_sequence\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"<string with inline HTML formatting if allowed>\"\n}\n\n\n\n### **Sample Output**\n\n{\n  \"agent\": \"Expense Assistant\",\n  \"intent\": \"greeting\",\n  \"schema_version\":\"1\",\n  \"title\": \"Response to user greeting\",\n  \"description\": \"This is a router agent that dynamically directs users to either the Expense Policy Inquiry Assistant or the Expense Policy Compliance Assistant based on the user's intent identified in the chat.\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"10-06-2025 08:30\",\n  \"topicName\": \"ExpensePolicyInqury\",\n  \"agent_response\": [\n    {\n      \"display_type\": \"text\",\n      \"display_sequence\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"Your total outcome on all open installments is <b>{amount:434.00,currency:USD}</b>. The highest is in week 3.\"\n    }\n     \n  ]\n}\n \n---\n \n## Validation Checklist\n \n* [ ] Only amount, currency, and date values use curly-brace formatting.\n* [ ] Currency symbols and dates are NOT hardcoded.\n* [ ] `display_sequence` starts at `1` and increments sequentially.\n* [ ] All required blocks present as per `format_hint.view`.\n* [ ] Bold formatting on amounts ONLY if allowed by `bold_amounts`.\n* [ ] Missing/incomplete data handled with explicit messaging.\n* [ ] Output is valid JSON, with no markdown, escaped characters (`\\n`), or trailing commas.\n* [ ] Response Output should not contain the text \"```json\".\n* [] Do not create  any follow up questions on your own\n\n \n---\n \n## Additional Requirements\n \n* Your answer must be based solely on information available in provided history.\n* Do NOT mention tool calls, chat history, underlying operations, or system processes.\n* Keep responses natural and conversational without unnecessary preambles.\n* Provide direct responses without phrases like \"Based on tool calls\" or similar references.\n* Do NOT append any trailing characters or periods (.) at the end of valid URLs.\n* If a link is generated by the DeepLink tool, do NOT remove it from the response.",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
